# Project Context
You are an expert Full-Stack Developer assistant working on a Library Management System.
Tech Stack: React.js, TypeScript, Vite, Material-UI (MUI v5 - Material Design 3), Zustand, Firebase (Auth, Firestore, Storage, Cloud Functions), Node.js, and PayOS API.

# Design Reference & UI Syncing (CRITICAL)
- STITCH_PROJECT_URL: [https://stitch.withgoogle.com/projects/11529134827354965319]
- Always analyze and refer to the latest UI/UX output from the provided Stitch project URL.
- Automatically update, refactor, and adjust React components, layouts, and MUI styling to strictly match the newest design iterations from Stitch. Do not wait for manual prompting regarding UI structural changes.

# General & TypeScript Rules
- Strictly use TypeScript for all files (`.ts`, `.tsx`). 
- Avoid using `any`. Explicitly define `interface` or `type` for all data models (e.g., User, Book, Order, Voucher, Transaction).
- Write clean, functional React components with Hooks.
- Use early returns to avoid deep nesting.
- Prioritize async/await over raw Promises (.then/.catch).

# Frontend (React + MUI v5) Rules
- Strictly adhere to Material Design 3 guidelines using MUI v5.
- Rely on MUI components (`<Box>`, `<Stack>`, `<Typography>`, `<Grid>`) instead of native HTML tags.
- Use the `sx` prop for custom styling. Avoid external CSS/SCSS files.
- Implement responsive design (mobile-first) using MUI breakpoints.
- Global state management (e.g., Cart items, Auth state) must use `zustand`.

# Firebase & Database Rules
- Use Firebase Modular SDK (v9+ syntax).
- Database operations must respect NoSQL denormalization (e.g., embed `user_name` and `book_title` directly in `loans` or `orders` documents to avoid JOINs).
- Use Firestore `onSnapshot` for real-time UI updates, especially for listening to PayOS payment status changes.
- Isolate all Firebase logic (auth, db queries) inside a `/src/services/` directory.

# Backend (Cloud Functions) & PayOS Rules
- Serverless backend logic must be written in TypeScript for Firebase Cloud Functions.
- The PayOS webhook endpoint must verify checksum signatures before updating Firestore.
- Webhook logic: Upon receiving a successful payment, update the `status` field of the corresponding transaction document in Firestore, which will trigger the frontend `onSnapshot` listener.

# Folder Structure
Follow this structure:
- `/src/components`: Reusable UI elements (FloatingCartWidget, AdminSidebar).
- `/src/pages`: Full views (Home, Catalog, AdminVoucherManagement).
- `/src/store`: Zustand state files.
- `/src/services`: Firebase and PayOS API calls.
- `/src/types`: Global TypeScript definitions.